  "why": "Cross-type rule (operator, 2026-09-26; compare-spec 2.16.0): an Episode with a USER-SUPPLIED title whose SERIES is classed Anthology is a candidate for a Basic record -- scored on the Basic profile and capped into Review, never auto-matched. The episode itself carries no class and runs 25 minutes, so neither the Pilot/Special/Standalone rule nor the feature-length rule (2.19.0) can make it eligible: ONLY the Series' class can, and the Series is neither the submission nor the candidate. It arrives through the `ancestry` block (specs/golden-pairs.md section 2; De-Dupe UI S-32), and an implementation that cannot climb to it -- or ignores the block -- scores the pair as ineligible (Reject) and FAILS this fixture loudly, as the format requires. Shape: an anthology play broadcast as an episode and later listed as a stand-alone short.",
